  "answer":"No. The current release policy does not allow a model to be released based solely on accuracy exceeding 0.80. Production model changes must be evaluated on a frozen holdout set and can only be promoted when the F1 score improves by at least 0.005 and the ROC‑AUC does not drop by more than 0.01. The older rule that allowed promotion when accuracy was above 0.80 is explicitly superseded by this policy.",
  "sources":[
